              "type": "History and Physical",
              "title": "New Patient Physical",
              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2021-06-22T08:35",
              "body": "32 y/o M establishing care. Prior PCP retired; last physical roughly 2018 per pt, nothing abnormal that he recalls. Records requested.\n\nNo complaints. Runs 3-4 mornings a week, demonstrates drills with his teams, no limitation.\n\nPMH: none. PSH: none. Meds: none. Allergies: NKDA.\nImmunizations: COVID Pfizer x2 this spring (card seen). Tdap unknown date - given today.\n\nFamily hx: father had emphysema diagnosed at 42 and died at 48 of cirrhosis, which the family put down to his drinking. Paternal uncle has COPD. Paternal grandmother had cirrhosis, cause never found.\n\nSocial: teaches PE at the high school, coaches varsity. Lives with his partner. Never smoked. Alcohol a drink or two a month. No drugs.\n\nROS negative except as above.\n\nExam: vitals as charted, BMI ~22. Well-appearing, fit. HEENT normal, no thyromegaly or nodes. Lungs clear to auscultation throughout, good air movement. RRR, no murmur. Abdomen soft, nontender, no hepatosplenomegaly. Skin unremarkable. No edema.\n\nPHQ-2 0.\n\nA/P: Healthy adult, preventive visit.\n- CBC, CMP, lipid panel; one-time HIV and hep C screen\n- Tdap today\n- Flu shot this fall\n- Family hx of early emphysema in a drinker father noted; he has no symptoms. Revisit if anything changes.\nRTC 1 yr."
            }
